#slide[
  = Motivation: The Curse of Dimensionality

  *Why reduce dimensions in multivariate data?*

  - *High Collinearity:* Redundant predictors destabilize regression and inference.
  - *Interpretability:* Condense dozens of observed indicators into underlying constructs.
  - *Visualization:* Project $p$-dimensional data onto 2D or 3D coordinate planes.
  - *Noise Reduction:* Separate shared systematic signal from item-specific measurement noise.

  #v(0.8em)

  #grid(
    columns: (1fr, 1fr),
